<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rubenid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1080–<a href="/years/1219">1219</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Roupenians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rubenid dynasty was an Armenian ruling family named after its founder Ruben I, who established a lordship in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus</a> mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> around 1080. His descendants extended their power over the Cilician plain, and in 1198 Leo I was crowned king, founding the Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia. The male line ended with Leo's death in 1219, and his daughter Zabel's marriage brought the crown to the Hethumids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rubenid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Rubenid dynasty" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Rubenid_Dynasty.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
